creates a j2ee compliant application deployment descriptor.

you first need to set up a directory structure like this:

stage
stage/javas
stage/javas/jcan-log.jar
stage/javas/logon-common.jar
stage/javas/log4j-1.2.8.jar
stage/javas/commons-lang-2.3.jar
stage/javas/logon-business-client.jar
stage/ejbs
stage/ejbs/logon-business.jar
stage/wars
stage/wars/tablebrowser
stage/wars/tablebrowser/logon-webapp.war

the generator will then create an application.xml according to this scructure.

- the ejbs are in 'ejbs'
- jar files which are shared by all modules are in 'javas'
- the web apps are in wars
    - the wars dir contains directories
    - these directories' names will be taken as the context root of the webapp
      which resides inside those directories.
